 :question/id #uuid "2c2bce04-d1e3-5f1d-bdce-22472d9c21e5"] [:db/add "2c2bce04-d1e3-5f1d-bdce-22472d9c21e5" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{2}{9 x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant."] [:db/add "2c2bce04-d1e3-5f1d-bdce-22472d9c21e5" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=\\frac{3 x}{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{3}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n9 x^{2} + 4=4\\left(1+(\\frac{3 x}{2})^2\\right).\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=\\frac{2}{3}\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{1}{3}$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{2}{9 x^{2} + 4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{u^{2} + 1}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{3 x}{2} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$"] [:db/add "2c2bce04-d1e3-5f1d-bdce-22472d9c21e5" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard] [:db/add "2c2bce04-d1e3-5f1d-bdce-22472d9c21e5" :question/answer-fields "b8613995-bd94-5b2a-8266-024798cec93f"] [:db/ensure "2c2bce04-d1e3-5f1d-bdce-22472d9c21e5" :question/validate] [:db/add 17592186064219 :knowledge-point/questions "2c2bce04-d1e3-5f1d-bdce-22472d9c21e5"] [:db/add "eef61d63-a43b-5994-9256-12c87331a530" :answer/id #uuid "eef61d63-a43b-5994-9256-12c87331a530"] [:db/add "eef61d63-a43b-5994-9256-12c87331a530" :answer/type :answer.type/math] [:db/add "eef61d63-a43b-5994-9256-12c87331a530" :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}\\left(\\arctan{\\left(\\frac{4 x}{3} \\right)}\\right)+C"] [:db/ensure "eef61d63-a43b-5994-9256-12c87331a530" :answer/validate]